Done. Implemented in scratch worktree `/tmp/cc1-exclude-callsites` (from `origin/master`, uncommitted).

**Part B — exclude from hashed manifest**

- [publish.cljc](/tmp/cc1-exclude-callsites/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc): `publish-closure!` materializes the manifest first with only the closed schema-1 keys, then builds the record `{:yang.call-site/schema 1 :yang.call-site/manifest manifest-address :yang.call-site/root (:root tree) :yang.call-site/origin origin :yang.call-site/table table-address}` and returns `:call-sites {:record :table :origin :root :manifest}` from `publish-module!`. `published-call-site-table` now accepts a record address, a `publish-module!` result, or `(handle manifest-address record-address)`, validating `:yang.call-site/manifest` against the manifest asked about, plus root and origin.
- [linker.cljc](/tmp/cc1-exclude-callsites/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc): reverted `:yin.module/call-sites` from `manifest-keys`/`manifest-defect`; schema-1 is the closed 10-key set again.
- [closure.cljc](/tmp/cc1-exclude-callsites/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc): removed `walk-call-sites` from `walk-manifest`.

**Part A — canonicalize row ordering**

- Added `jing/canonical-compare` (unsigned byte-wise order over `jing/canonical-bytes`) in [jing.cljc](/tmp/cc1-exclude-callsites/src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc), and replaced `sort-by pr-str` with it in [publish.cljc](/tmp/cc1-exclude-callsites/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc) `call-site-claim`, [clojure.cljc](/tmp/cc1-exclude-callsites/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc) `call-site-metadata`, and [macro.cljc](/tmp/cc1-exclude-callsites/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc) at the correspondence sort and `final-call-site-metadata`.

**Test update**

- Only [clojure_callsite_test.cljc](/tmp/cc1-exclude-callsites/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc): `published-module-test` now asserts the manifest excludes `:yin.module/call-sites`, the record names the manifest, identical specs under different scopes share one address `(= (:address via-a) (:address via-b))` with distinct `:record`/`:origin`/`:table`, and the side table travels only when carried explicitly. Retrieval call sites in `publisher-scope-admission-identity-test` were mechanically switched to the new result/record form.

**Protected files untouched**: `dht-import-v1.edn`, `linked_prelude_test.cljc`, `yang.core.call/module-uast`, and `test/yang/call/conformance.clj` — confirmed by `git diff --name-only`.

